.TH SDL_CreateGPURenderer 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_CreateGPURenderer \- Create a 2D GPU rendering context.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_Renderer * SDL_CreateGPURenderer(SDL_GPUDevice *device, SDL_Window *window);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The GPU device to use is passed in as a parameter\[char46] If this is NULL, then a device will be created normally and can be retrieved using
.BR SDL_GetGPURendererDevice ()\[char46]
.PP
The window to use is passed in as a parameter\[char46] If this is NULL, then this will become an offscreen renderer\[char46] In that case, you should call
.BR SDL_SetRenderTarget ()
to setup rendering to a texture, and then call
.BR SDL_RenderPresent ()
normally to complete drawing a frame\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I device
the GPU device to use with the renderer, or NULL to create a device\[char46]
.TP
.I window
the window where rendering is displayed, or NULL to create an offscreen renderer\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a valid rendering context or NULL if there was an error; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
If this function is called with a valid GPU device, it should be called on the thread that created the device\[char46] If this function is called with a valid window, it should be called on the thread that created the window\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

